+# Initial trial evidence
+
+2026-10-02. The initial proposal is a documentation baseline, not an adopted schema.
+
+Checks: manually traced both retrieval questions, zero-result retrieval, stable
+identity, second-participant and multiple/missing-service counterexamples. Reviewed
+ER endpoints against A1–A2 and terminology against the glossary. Checked 12 local links across 5 documents; all targets exist and no
+anchors are used. `git diff --check` passed. The documentation-only link checker
+used `python3` after the `python` alias was unavailable.
+
+Rendering limitation: repository inventory exposed no renderer or package setup;
+`command -v mmdc` returned no executable. Mermaid was reviewed as source only;
+parse, rendered readability, target-width and theme checks remain unverified.
+No dependencies were installed and no network or application runtime was used.
+
+Material friction: creating a two-edge ER diagram routed through project-docs,
+shared authoring, visual entrypoint, ER, composition, drawing and verification
+references. Much of composition and drawing discusses large flowcharts and
+subgraphs unused here. The reading cost was concrete; no instructions conflicted.
+A possible future improvement is a compact small-ER route, but this trial makes
+no changes to installed guidance.
